[41.991197, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d[demo] pre-checkpoint: workflow reached WORKFLOW_EXECUTION_STATUS_COMPLETED\u001b[3X\r\n[demo] pre-checkpoint: Activity attempts observed while the retry gap was open\u001b[4;78H\u001b[1K\r: 1, 2\r\n[demo] pre-checkpoint: evidence written to out/run-artifacts/pre-checkpoint/\u001b[2X\u001b[6;78H\u001b[1K\r\n=========================================================================\u001b[5X\r\n=== worker-kill demo: invariant report ===\u001b[36X\u001b[9;78H\u001b[1K\r\n  What this proves: a local fixture reproduction of the boundary.\u001b[13X\r\n  What it does not prove: production rollout. The unit converted here\u001b[9X\r\n  is proved by a bounded canary and runs in shadow; the part running\u001b[10X\r\n  continuously in production is result delivery and acknowledgement.\u001b[10X\u001b[14;78H\u001b[1K\r\n  Both arms are one result. Arm 1 passes even against a resolver that\u001b[9X\r\n  mints a duplicate session on every call, because its retry resumes\u001b[10X\r\n  from a checkpoint and never re-resolves. Only arm 2 shows that a\u001b[12X\r\n  duplicate launch was prevented. Do not present arm 1 on its own.\u001b[12X\u001b[19;78H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r--- arm: mid-execute ---\r\n    Worker killed mid-work; retry resumed from the checkpoint\u001b[17X\r\n    workflow : bead-orchestration/demo-city/worker-kill-demo/work-item-1\u001b[6X\r\n    activity : formula/demo-root/edit-file.author/g1\u001b[26X\u001b[24;78H\u001b[1K\r    session  : agent-session-9d3fdd31\r\n    receipt  : status=completed outcome=completed\u001b[29X\u001b[26;78H\u001b[1K\r\n    [PASS] proof 1: the bound session identity did not change across attempts\u001b[1X\r\n           distinct session identities seen by the agent adapter = 1\u001b[10X\r\n    [PASS] proof 1: the work store recorded that same session\u001b[17X\r\n           store session matches the one the agent bound = True\u001b[15X\r\n    [PASS] proof 2: exactly one session was created for this work item and gen\u001b[32;78H\u001b[1K\reration\u001b[33;78H\u001b[1K\r           session creations = 1\r\n    [PASS] proof 2: exactly one session record exists on disk for that pair\u001b[3X\u001b[35;78H\u001b[1K\r           session records = 1\r\n    [PASS] proof 3: exactly one terminal receipt was written to the work store\r\n           receipts = 1, status = completed\u001b[35X\r\n    [PASS] proof 3: the agent session produced one terminal record, not two\u001b[3X\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
[41.991328, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;1H    workflow : bead-orchestration/demo-city/worker-kill-demo-resolve/work-item\u001b[3;78H\u001b[1K\r-1\r\n    activity : formula/demo-root/edit-file.author/g1\u001b[26X\u001b[5;78H\u001b[1K\r    session  : agent-session-935ad273\r\n    receipt  : status=completed outcome=completed\u001b[29X\u001b[7;78H\u001b[1K\r\n    [PASS] proof 1: the bound session identity did not change across attempts\u001b[1X\r\n           distinct session identities seen by the agent adapter = 1\u001b[10X\r\n    [PASS] proof 1: the work store recorded that same session\u001b[17X\r\n           store session matches the one the agent bound = True\u001b[15X\r\n    [PASS] proof 2: exactly one session was created for this work item and gen\u001b[13;78H\u001b[1K\reration\u001b[14;78H\u001b[1K\r           session creations = 1\r\n    [PASS] proof 2: exactly one session record exists on disk for that pair\u001b[3X\u001b[16;78H\u001b[1K\r           session records = 1\r\n    [PASS] proof 3: exactly one terminal receipt was written to the work store\r\n           receipts = 1, status = completed\u001b[35X\r\n    [PASS] proof 3: the agent session produced one terminal record, not two\u001b[3X\u001b[20;78H\u001b[1K\r           agent terminal records = 1\r\n    [PASS] proof 3: a completion carrying the stale claim token failed closed\u001b[1X\r\n           rejection = 'stale bead generation or claim token'\u001b[17X\r\n    [PASS] the retry ran under the same Activity identity\u001b[21X\r\n           activity identities in history = ['formula/demo-root/edit-file.auth\u001b[25;78H\u001b[1K\ror/g1']\r\n    [PASS] Temporal really did retry (attempt two or later finished the work)\u001b[1X\n\u001b[1K\r           final attempt = 2\r\n    [PASS] the workflow closed on its own terms\u001b[31X\u001b[29;78H\u001b[1K\r           status = Completed\r\n    [PASS] arm fact: no checkpoint survived, so the retry had to ask the resol\u001b[31;78H\u001b[1K\rver again\u001b[32;78H\u